## 16. Humor and tone

The register is deadpan, corporate and analytics. One image carries two readings. The second reading rewards a deliberate look.

### Rules

1. Jokes target observed behavior: posting, reposting, ratios, moderation.
2. Jokes never sit on the gameplay read path. A signal (LIVE, Stan, Go Viral, Ratio) is always readable without its joke.
3. Voice is calm and under-acted. Nothing shouts except the Hot Take archetype, and that is also a joke.
4. Gags are frequency-controlled. The player can turn every gag off.

### Gags

| # | Gag | System | Trigger | Fade or opt-out |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 01 | Loading fold-in: two outer panels slide together, revealing the first Trend modifier. Caption: What is everyone talking about this match? | The Trend | Every load | Skippable. Static in Reduced Motion. |
| 02 | Stan signs: hand-lettered signs held by buffed creeps, naming the buffing hero with a misspelling that rotates each match | Stan and Reach | Zoom or spectator camera | Signs stay. Misspelling rotates. |
| 03 | Via shrinkage: each Repost link adds a small via tag. By the fifth link the original is too small to read. | Repost | Chain of 3 or more | Spectator and hover only |
| 04 | Death recap as analytics: header Your post was ratioed. Killers listed as Top replies. Line: Engagement redistributed: 50%. | Ratio | Death | Standard damage table first. Header toggleable. |
| 05 | Rebrand nameplate: hero name followed by a small grey formerly tag | Rebrand | Buyback | 3 s, nameplate only |
| 06 | Go Private blinds: windows show the padlock and the blinds drop. One slat stays bent open. | Go Private | Activation | Cosmetic. The padlock is the read. |
| 07 | Stale Trend husk: the expired modifier's costume lies in the pit until the Trend respawns | The Trend | Kill | Fades on respawn |
| 08 | Out-of-bounds margins: a creep sits on grass with eyes closed. A lone tree carries a no signal glyph. | Map edge | Camera at edge | Static and silent |
| 09 | Item flavor lines in deadpan (section 11) | Items | Tooltip hover | Hidden in compact tooltips |
| 10 | Analytics idle: a hero who is not LIVE and has stood still for 8 s glances at a grey rectangle, then puts it away | Absence of LIVE | 8 s idle while unseen | Max once per 60 s. Never while LIVE. |
| 11 | Recommended banner: appears on a lane the algorithm favors, reading Recommended for you, with Based on your activity in small print | Lane notice | Lane selection | Small print |
| 12 | Courier failure: a faded speech bubble with an ellipsis that never resolves | Courier | Courier death | Fades in 4 s |
| 13 | Tower rubble: a sign on the debris reads This thread has been locked. | Towers | Tower death | Removed at +2 min |
| 14 | Victory and defeat fold: click and hold reveals the losing Original Post as \[deleted\] | Original Post | End screen | Requires a click. Clean stats view is the default. |
| 15 | Go Viral shadow counter: the hero's own shadow shows a ticking follower count | Go Viral | Activation | Self and allies only. Reduced opacity. |

### Announcer lines

| Event | Line |
| --- | --- |
| First blood | First reply. |
| Kill streak, three | This is going around. |
| Kill streak, five | Trending. |
| Clout reaches 100 | The algorithm noticed. |
| Ratio on death | Ratioed. |
| Tower destroyed | Thread locked. |
| Screenshot revive | Everyone gets one. |
| Rebrand | Under new management. |
| The Trend killed | Trending number one. |
| Original Post destroyed | Post deleted. |
| Victory screen | Your post performed well. |
| Defeat screen | Your post has been archived. |

Each event has a pool of three to five lines. The Plain announcer option uses the same events with plain lines.

### Settings

| Setting | Effect |
| --- | --- |
| Gag frequency: Full | All gags |
| Gag frequency: Reduced | Marginalia and tooltips kept. Voice quips and animated gags removed. |
| Gag frequency: Off | None |
| Plain announcer | Announcer uses the plain register |
| Analytics framing | Toggles the death-recap header |
| Reduced motion | Removes the loading fold-in animation and screen shake |

## 17. Presentation and readability

Every gameplay signal passes three tests: it reads in grayscale, at gameplay zoom, and at minimap size.

### Size targets

| Element | Author size | Minimum display | Test |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Ability icon | 128 × 128 PNG | 32 px | Motif identifiable in grayscale. Fills 60 to 75% of frame. Bottom-right 25% clear for cooldown numbers. |
| Item icon | 88 × 64 PNG; 176 × 128 master | 44 × 32 | One object, ¾ view, rim light, no text |
| Status icon | 64 × 64 | 18 px | Single glyph in system color with 2 px dark outline |
| Minimap hero icon | 32 × 32 (64 master) | 16 px | Head-only caricature reads as a solid silhouette |
| Hero model | Gameplay zoom, 60 to 90 px tall |  | Silhouette identifies hero and facing, 90% or better in a blind test |
| Value groups |  |  | At least 3 per hero. Head and prop at least 30% luminance delta from body. |
| UI text contrast |  |  | 4.5:1 or better on HUD panels |
| Status glyph against health bar |  |  | 3:1 or better |
| Cast point | 0.2 to 0.5 s |  | Anticipation pose readable top-down. Unique per ability. |
| Death animation | 2.0 s or less |  |  |
| AoE telegraph | Team-colored decal |  | Outline at true radius. Fill at 25% opacity or less. |

### Hero shape language

| Shape | Meaning | Detail zone |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Circle | Support, friendly | Head, shoulders and signature prop carry about 70% of detail and saturation. Lower body is low-saturation rest. |
| Square | Durable | Same detail rule. Chest and shoulders carry the read. |
| Triangle | Aggressive, mobile | Silhouette point (weapon, hood, hair) carries the read. |

### Color system

| Meaning | Color | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Ally team, Morning Feed | #2E8BFF | Light-value structures. Teams also differ in value. |
| Enemy team, Late Night Feed | #FF8A1F | Dark-value structures |
| Self | White and gold outline | Yellow health bar |
| Clout, all Clout UI and VFX | #A35CFF | Reserved for Clout only |
| LIVE | Violet dot, white ring | Never red |
| Damage and danger | #D9534F | Flashing elements stay below R/(R+G+B) of 0.8 |
| Heal and buff | #3DDC97 | Paired with an upward chevron |
| Debuff | Shape only | Inverted chevron |

Rules:

- Every color signal carries a shape. Ally creeps have rounded hoods. Enemy creeps have angular hoods.
- Colorblind presets: deuteranopia, protanopia, tritanopia, and a custom picker.
- Red is never used for a non-damage signal. LIVE and Clout are never red.

### UI

- Top bar: Clout bar and follower count. Abbreviated 1.2K and 3.4M, exact on hover.
- Scoreboard: K, D, A, Clout, Net Worth. Tooltips: Engagement and Impressions.
- Tooltips: mechanical text first, italic flavor second. 14 px minimum.
- Cursor: four states (default, attack, ability target, invalid). 32 × 32.
- Minimap: Trend timer and Go Viral overlays.

